ID: vr-66
Title: Actual Mark model in the shared speaking-head runtime

Status: DONE
Milestone: Consistent native speaking heads
Dependencies: vr-51, vr-65

Purpose:
  Make the pinned actual Mark network, PCA and native head available as a
  first-class model with the shared presentation and interaction controls.

Tasks:
  Select Mark before loading weights; retain its native conditioning/input.
  Parse pinned scene numerical arrays only and retain Mark's native identity.
  Calibrate shared framing, features, optics and optional procedural hair.
  Add Mark to lightweight catalogs, manager, CLI and agent-facing contracts.
  Qualify generation, all emotions/controls, cancellation and selected loading.

Acceptance criteria:
  Selecting Mark loads Mark's network and 272-component PCA, not Claire's
    network or the preserved Male-SharpJawline sculpt.
  Mark supports the shared face views, neck/crop, zoom/orientation/cursor,
    colors, optional hair, natural blinking and emotion/cheekiness controls.
  Original geometry and learned motion are preserved up to the documented
    similarity transform and finite packing error.
  Existing models and idle-manager lightweight loading remain correct.
  No downloads, scene execution, devices or changes to protected sessions.

Completion evidence:
  Actual Mark v2.3 network,272-component skin PCA and native conditioning are
    selected before loading. Native geometry is similarity-aligned, not Claire.
  88 CPU regressions, actual six-model native sessions03 and final actual Mark
